  "articleBody": "When you're looking at a foreclosed property, what you see on the surface might just be the tip of the iceberg. Hidden damage is super common in these homes, and it's crucial to know what to look for and how to approach it. Often, neglect or vacancy can lead to serious issues that aren't immediately obvious. We're talking about things like water damage that's been covered up, or structural issues lurking behind drywall. The first step is always a thorough inspection — you want to check the structure, utilities, and moisture levels before anything else. It's smart to assume there's more going on than meets the eye, so budget for the unexpected. Things like old electrical systems, plumbing failures, or even widespread mold from long-term vacancy are frequent culprits. Don't start with cosmetic fixes before you've got a handle on the bigger, underlying problems. Getting a professional opinion right from the start can help you prioritize repairs and avoid costly mistakes. We're here to help you uncover and address these hidden challenges, making sure your renovation is built on a solid foundation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}